@startuml variant-decision-tree
' Decision tree for choosing a duallity WFST variant. Leaves = variants (duallity blue #D6EAF8).
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam activity {
  DiamondBackgroundColor #EAECEE
  DiamondBorderColor #707B7C
  DiamondFontColor #2C3E50
  ArrowColor #34495E
  BorderColor #34495E
  BackgroundColor #FDEBD0
}
title Which WFST variant? — a decision tree over duallity's exports

start
:Choosing a duallity WFST variant;
if (Phonetic / sound-alike match?) then (yes)
  if (Mapping given as rules or a regex?) then (fixed rewrite rules)
    :**RewriteWfst**
    rule rewrites (ph->f, ck->k)
    no feature gate; <<#D6EAF8>>
    stop
  else (phonetic regex)
    :**PhoneticWfst** / **PhoneticNfaWfst**
    compiled Thompson NFA
    feature "phonetic-rules"; <<#D6EAF8>>
    stop
  endif
else (no)
  if (k large over a big dictionary?) then (yes)
    :**WallBreakerWfst**
    pigeonhole seeds via SCDAWG
    bidirectional extension; <<#D6EAF8>>
    stop
  else (no)
    if (Many queries, same dict and k?) then (yes)
      :**UniversalLevenshteinWfst**
      query-agnostic automaton
      built once per max_distance; <<#D6EAF8>>
      stop
    else (no)
      if (Runtime-configurable op set?) then (yes)
        :**GeneralizedWfst**
        OperationSet: standard / transposition /
        merge-split / phonetic-digraph; <<#D6EAF8>>
        stop
      else (no)
        :**LevenshteinWfst**
        the core adapter — start here; <<#D6EAF8>>
        stop
      endif
    endif
  endif
endif

legend bottom
  Blue leaves are duallity WFST variants; every one implements Wfst<char, TropicalWeight>,
  so any choice remains composable via compose(t1, t2). Diamonds are decisions.
end legend
@enduml
